                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1409-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ></span>Audix M44</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Detachable-Capsule Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The Audix M44 is a miniature condenser microphone for drum and percussion capture. It is a modular microphone, equipped with either a Cardioid or Hypercardioid capsule (model M44-HC).</p><p>The condenser elements are minature electrets, cited as 12mm although actually measuring 10mm in diameter. They have high SPL capability (150dB at 0.5% THD), low sensitivity (3mV/Pa), and, predictably, high self-noise (25dBA). Given these specs, the seem best suited to close-miking loud sources such as horns and percussion.</p><p>The mic is terminated with mini-XLR jack. A 25&#39; mini-XLR-F to XLR-M cable is supplied.</p><p>It ships with:</p><ul><li>25&#39; cable with mini-XLRf - XLRm connectors (CBL-M25)</li><li>Mic stand adapter (MC-MICRO)</li><li>Lug mount adapted for hand percussion instruments with shockmount</li><li>ring (DCLAMP-MICRO)</li><li>Drum rim mount attachment with shockmount ring (DVICE-MICRO) External foam windscreen (WS10)</li><li>Carrying pouch (P1)</li></ul><p><p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Audix/M44">Audix M44</a> is also known as: M44-HC.</p>
